# GitHub & commits (client)

Repo: `minhduy6868/peer_task_client`. Default branch: `dev`.

- Branch: `feat/<slug>`, `fix/<slug>`, `chore/<slug>`, `docs/<slug>`, `refactor/<slug>`.
- Commits: Conventional Commits, English, imperative, **why** not file lists.

```
feat(board): persist stroke ops after peer sync
fix(auth): refresh access token before retrying 401
```

Scopes: `auth`, `workspace`, `board`, `task`, `p2p`, `ui`, `l10n`, `offline`.
- One concern per commit. Never `--no-verify`, force-push `dev`/`main`, or commit `.env`.
- PR into `dev`: title = same as commit style. Body: Summary + Test plan. Use `gh pr create` from `client/`.
- Do not include `server/` files in this repo’s commits.

## Ship

The user asked that each finished fix is committed, pushed, and deployed. Do that without asking again.

1. Commit only this repo, Conventional Commits, one concern each.
2. `git push origin HEAD`.
3. Fast-forward `main` (`git push origin HEAD:main`) when it is a fast-forward, so production updates.
4. Push to `main` runs `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, which publishes https://peertask.pages.dev when `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` is set. If that job fails because the secret is missing, publish with the local Wrangler login. Do not publish twice after Actions succeeds.
5. Skip secrets, questions, and reviews. If `main` cannot fast-forward, say so and do not force-push.
